# Dependencies and scope

Work one authorized task.

- Name its ledger ID when one was given, its hard dependency, and whether that dependency is verified in the current code.
- Do not start a task whose dependency is still unverified.
- Do not invent a task ID or mix AB labels, MASTER labels, and prompt numbers.
- If the change needs files outside the authorized scope, stop and report the blocker.
- Do not delete dormant modules. Gate unused behavior only when the task asks, and keep the route, API, and job from running while the flag is off.
- A ledger phase blocks the next phase until recorded evidence exists. A described feature is not an implemented dependency.
